  "statement": "Find the first four terms in the expansion of $(1+2x)^{1/2}$ in ascending powers of $x$.",
  "solution": "$$(1+u)^{1/2}=1+\\tfrac12u+\\frac{(\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac12)}{2!}u^{2}+\\frac{(\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac12)(-\\tfrac32)}{3!}u^{3}+\\cdots.$$\nWith $u=2x$:\n\\begin{align*}\n(1+2x)^{1/2}&=1+\\tfrac12(2x)+\\left(-\\tfrac18\\right)(2x)^{2}+\\left(\\tfrac18\\right)(2x)^{3}+\\cdots\\\\\n&=1+x-\\tfrac12x^{2}+\\tfrac12x^{3}+\\cdots.\n\\end{align*}",
  "solutionStatus": "full",
  "hints": [
    "Use the general binomial expansion with n = 1/2.",
    "Substitute u = 2x term by term.",
    "Simplify the numerical coefficients."
